WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.050
When an alarm goes off, the first question on the

00:07.050 --> 00:10.537
surface is simple: who is underground right now?

00:10.537 --> 00:13.025
Nobody can answer it from memory. The answer has

00:13.025 --> 00:15.575
to come from the check-in and check-out record.

00:15.575 --> 00:18.438
Get it wrong, and rescuers either search for someone

00:18.438 --> 00:21.050
who's already safe at home, or worse,

00:21.050 --> 00:23.512
nobody looks for someone who's still inside.

00:24.649 --> 00:26.623
The standard for underground mines,

00:26.623 --> 00:31.949
30 CFR 57.11058, says every operator has to set

00:31.949 --> 00:34.623
up a check-in and check-out system that gives an

00:34.623 --> 00:36.899
accurate record of the people in the mine.

00:36.899 --> 00:39.724
The record is kept on the surface, in a place chosen

00:39.724 --> 00:42.711
to protect it from fire or other hazards.

00:42.711 --> 00:45.524
And every person underground has to carry a positive

00:45.524 --> 00:47.411
means of being identified.

00:48.534 --> 00:51.947
At all of our sites, that system is the tag board.

00:51.947 --> 00:54.547
Boonesboro and Clover Bottom also have a separate

00:54.547 --> 00:57.334
check-in for visitors, and at Boonesboro that includes

00:57.334 --> 01:00.234
contractors. If you bring a visitor or a delivery

01:00.234 --> 01:02.659
driver near the mine, make sure they've checked

01:02.659 --> 01:04.384
in the way the site requires.

01:05.496 --> 01:08.459
The rules for your tag are short. Tag in every

01:08.459 --> 01:11.058
time you go underground, and tag out every time

01:11.058 --> 01:13.308
you come out, even if you're only going up to the

01:13.308 --> 01:16.171
shop for a part. Move only your own tag.

01:16.171 --> 01:18.784
Never tag in or out for someone else,

01:18.784 --> 01:21.571
even as a favor, because then the board is wrong

01:21.571 --> 01:22.984
and nobody knows it.

01:24.114 --> 01:26.339
Most board mistakes aren't on purpose.

01:26.339 --> 01:28.752
Someone comes out at the end of a long shift and

01:28.752 --> 01:31.339
forgets to tag out, so the board says he's still

01:31.339 --> 01:35.014
underground. Someone loses a tag and goes in anyway.

01:35.014 --> 01:37.964
A visitor or a delivery driver follows a crew in

01:37.964 --> 01:40.389
without checking in. Each one looks small on a

01:40.389 --> 01:44.014
normal day. In an emergency, each one sends people

01:44.014 --> 01:46.527
looking in the wrong place, or makes the person

01:46.527 --> 01:48.989
in charge decide whether to send rescuers into

01:48.989 --> 01:51.264
smoke for someone who's already home.

01:52.380 --> 01:55.705
If your tag is missing or damaged, don't go underground

01:55.705 --> 01:57.968
until you've told your supervisor and the record

01:57.968 --> 02:00.843
is right. If you notice a tag still on the IN side

02:00.843 --> 02:03.418
for someone you know is out, say so.

02:03.418 --> 02:05.943
Fixing the board is everybody's job.

02:09.262 --> 02:11.712
Clover Bottom has two separate mines that share

02:11.712 --> 02:14.850
one surface: the old mine, number one,

02:14.850 --> 02:18.362
and the new mine, number two. There's one tag board:

02:18.362 --> 02:21.174
in-mine number one on the left, out in the middle,

02:21.174 --> 02:23.150
and in-mine number two on the right.

02:23.150 --> 02:25.787
Each in-mine section is its own record,

02:25.787 --> 02:28.237
and the trailer it hangs on is signed Emergency

02:28.237 --> 02:31.525
Assembly Area 1. If you tag in under the old mine

02:31.525 --> 02:33.799
but work in the new one, the board says you're

02:33.799 --> 02:36.174
in the wrong place, and in a fire that's where

02:36.174 --> 02:37.650
people will look for you.

02:38.789 --> 02:41.639
This isn't a theory. From 2021 through our latest

02:41.639 --> 02:45.389
data, MSHA inspectors cited the check-in and check-out

02:45.389 --> 02:47.889
standard three times at Clover Bottom.

02:47.889 --> 02:49.914
The site's takeaway says it plainly:

02:49.914 --> 02:52.851
when two mines share one surface, everyone has

02:52.851 --> 02:54.251
to be accounted for.

02:57.578 --> 02:59.603
When you come out in an evacuation,

02:59.603 --> 03:01.778
go straight to the gathering point so you can be

03:01.778 --> 03:04.678
counted. The person in charge compares who's standing

03:04.678 --> 03:06.916
there with the tags still on the board.

03:06.916 --> 03:09.253
Don't go to your truck, don't go home,

03:09.253 --> 03:11.528
and don't wander off to check on equipment.

03:11.528 --> 03:13.216
If you leave before you're counted,

03:13.216 --> 03:15.503
you become a missing person on paper,

03:15.503 --> 03:17.728
and someone may risk going in after you.

03:17.728 --> 03:20.378
Every site's tag board is a gathering point.

03:20.378 --> 03:23.441
Boonesboro also uses an area behind the mine outside

03:23.441 --> 03:26.591
the 22 North escapeway, and Clover Bottom also

03:26.591 --> 03:29.603
uses the old mine entrance and the area behind

03:29.603 --> 03:32.378
the mine by the haul road to the asphalt plant.

03:33.513 --> 03:35.875
If someone is missing, tell the person in charge

03:35.875 --> 03:38.888
right away: who it is, where you last saw them,

03:38.888 --> 03:41.750
and when. Then stay put. Never go back in on your

03:41.750 --> 03:45.062
own. Going back in alone is how one missing miner

03:45.062 --> 03:47.975
becomes two. Re-entry is directed by the person

03:47.975 --> 03:50.812
in charge and done by people trained and equipped

03:50.812 --> 03:51.613
for it.

03:52.742 --> 03:54.667
It's hard to stand at the portal when a friend

03:54.667 --> 03:57.630
hasn't come out. Every instinct says go get him.

03:57.630 --> 04:00.067
But the smoke or bad air that slowed him down is

04:00.067 --> 04:02.755
still there, and your self-rescuer may already

04:02.755 --> 04:05.767
be used. The most useful thing you can do for him

04:05.767 --> 04:08.242
is give clear, accurate information,

04:08.242 --> 04:10.742
fast, and then be ready to help when the person

04:10.742 --> 04:12.130
in charge asks.

04:13.256 --> 04:16.244
So remember five things. Tag in and tag out every

04:16.244 --> 04:19.369
time. Move only your own tag. Tag in at the mine

04:19.369 --> 04:21.656
where you're working. In an evacuation,

04:21.656 --> 04:24.119
go to the gathering point and get counted.

04:24.119 --> 04:26.631
And if someone is missing, report it and never

04:26.631 --> 04:28.043
go back in alone.

04:29.162 --> 04:32.325
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

04:32.325 --> 04:33.825
override this video.
